{
  "id": 471367638,
  "iid": 24251,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "bthid: Fix dissection of packet header",
  "description": "The header of a BT HID packet is 1 byte in size and is comprised of two 4-bit fields: transaction/message type (upper 4 bits) and parameter (lower 4 bits). The commit c5933ad583d3a4c33af1bdc7bd4add9e8f8cafd8 attempted to remove one read from the TVB for the HID header. However, the header field used to read the HID header, hf_bthid_transaction_type, has a bit mask to exclude the lower 4 bits. The dissector then tries to extract the transaction type and parameter fields from the read value, but since only the upper 4 bits remain, the extracted fields are incorrect. This leads to the dissector mistaking every BT HID packet as a HANDSHAKE message.\n\nLet the new function for extracting the transaction type field read from the TVB and automatically apply the bit mask, but read from the TVB again to extract the parameter field.\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2026-04-07T18:18:18.412Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-04-07T21:10:15.530Z",
